 # Dynamic Scene and Temporal Modeling
 
-Also called: Dynamic NeRF, 4D Radiance Fields, Temporal NeRF
 
 ## Overview
-Dynamic Scene and Temporal Modeling adapts static NeRF architectures to handle time-varying scenes, addressing the ghosting and blurriness artifacts that occur when static models are applied to video data [S1][S2, unofficial]. It enables novel view synthesis at arbitrary times by modeling temporal variations in geometry and appearance [G]. This family differs from static NeRF variants by explicitly incorporating temporal coordinates or deformation fields to capture scene dynamics [G].
